notes="This leaf continues the partial-algebra discussion: sections C*(U), a graded algebra structure on their cohomology, and the comparison to H*(U,k_U). A pale sentence asserts multiplicativity; this run transcribes the assertion but does not claim a proof of the comparison theorem. Example 1 refers to an ordinary differential algebra; Example 2 has an exterior complex with multiplication by T and identifies cycles with exterior powers of Psi. Its hypotheses and the concluding parenthesis are among the least legible passages in the set and remain extensively marked. In the two-row display, C^n and Lambda^{n+1}Phi are supported by the raised ink, not H’s matching i degrees; the next top object appears to be C^{n+1} and is explicitly left doubtful. The identity (T wedge)(T wedge x)=0 follows from T wedge T=0 in an exterior algebra over any commutative base. That checks only the complex property, not the resolution claim or the displayed cycle identification, whose needed hypotheses cannot be securely recovered here. The initial hom label is (1), not a star. Manuscript foot 351; no date."
